    "title": "🤯 Bonkers idea: club in Brazil loans out manager - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By OneFootball ,\n21 hours ago\n🤯 Bonkers idea: club in Brazil loans out manager | Image credits : Getty Players who are loaned to another club — for example to gain match practice — are perfectly normal in the football business. Loans of this kind are part of everyday life.\nIn Brazil, however, a highly unusual loan deal has now caused a stir. Second-division side Criciúma EC have loaned in a coach. ‘Sky’ reports this.\nUmberto Louzer will take charge of the club until the end of the season. However, the 46-year-old will not be appointed permanently, but will instead join on loan from third-division side Guarani FC. The coach is still under contract there until the end of 2027.\nThe fact that he can work in the second division on a temporary basis is due to the different schedules of the leagues. The Série C season has already ended, while there are still nine matchdays left in Série B.\nUnlike in most European countries, the seasons in Brazil are played within a single calendar year.\nThis article was translated into English by Artificial Intelligence. You can read the original version in 🇩🇪 here.",
    "summary": "🤯 Bonkers idea: club in Brazil loans out manager | Image credits : Getty Players who are loaned to another club — for example to gain match practice — are perfectly normal in the football business. In Brazil, however, a highly unusual loan deal has now caused a stir. However, the 46-year-old will not be appointed permanently, but will instead join on loan from third-division side Guarani FC. The fact that he can work in the second division on a temporary basis is due to the different schedules of the leagues.",
